{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And he shall wash his flesh, etc.</b> Above we learned from ״וְרָחַץ אֶת בְּשָׂרוֹ וּלְבֵשָׁם״ that when he changes from golden garments to white garments he requires immersion — for in that immersion he stripped off the golden garments in which he had performed the morning daily service and dons white garments for the service of the day — and here we learn that when he changes from white garments to golden garments he requires immersion (Leviticus 16:32)." "<b>In a holy place.</b> That which is sanctified with the sanctity of the courtyard; and it was on the roof of the House of Parwah. And likewise the four immersions that are obligatory on that day [were there] — but the first was in unconsecrated ground (Leviticus 16:19)." "<b>And he shall put on his garments.</b> The eight garments in which he serves all the days of the year." "<b>And he shall go out.</b> From the Hekhal to the courtyard where the altar of burnt offering is." "<b>And he shall make his burnt offering.</b> The ram for a burnt offering mentioned above." "<b>And the burnt-offering of the people.</b> One ram for a burnt-offering, as stated above: ״וּמֵאֵת עֲדַת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ and so forth."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "The citation (שם י\"ט) likely refers to Yoma 3:6 or a related passage in the same chapter dealing with the location and number of immersions."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:52.976091028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}